ernal, from 1926 to 1948, and has been read by Western observers as a record of “efforts to form a national consciousness” (Rossi 1938: 569) and of “the institutionalization of the state” (Obermeyer 1981: 181).\'  So far, no mention of Ottoman postal systems has been made in the sources.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2415, 'temperature': 0.2})
